466	/****************************************************************************
467	 * Name: ai_watch_light_start
468	 *
469	 * Description:
470	 *   Spin up the ambient-light sampling thread. Split out of init on purpose.
471	 *
472	 *   The LCPU bring-up right after init (lcpu patch -> cal -> release) is
473	 *   timing-sensitive down to the microsecond, and the HCI commands that drive
474	 *   it are issued from the main thread. Whenever the main thread blocks in
475	 *   HAL_Delay_us() it gives the CPU away, and a 1 Hz I2C reader that is
476	 *   already running can land inside those gaps. Nothing here is urgent --
477	 *   the panel keeps the boot brightness until the first conversion -- so the
478	 *   thread waits until the radio is up (or has given up and scheduled a
479	 *   retry). Call this from the same thread that finishes BLE bring-up.
480	 *
481	 ****************************************************************************/
482	
